# MVP surface

Default work targets a closed/beta MVP of the core stack. Do not pull in deferred layers unless the user explicitly asks.

## In scope

- Identity create / 3-factor unlock (`@par-noir/identity-crypto`)
- Drive device-cloud custody + API owner routes
- Browse: public feeds, free follow, engagement
- Messaging: E2E DMs/groups (crypto via `@par-noir/dm-crypto`)
- OAuth unlock proofs (ML-DSA), no passcode on the wire

## Out of scope unless asked

- Veriff / identity verification product rails
- Stripe / creator fund / monetization go-live
- Platform paid feed subscriptions (already `410`)
- App Store / Play distribution
- Identity Drive re-key / succession migrate under custody (peer-credential allowlist debt)

## Bans (even inside MVP)

- New dual resolvers for Drive tokens or peer credentials
- Demo / stub crypto next to real PQC paths
- JSON format fallbacks when the primary Sheets/API path exists
- “Verify later” / trust-the-client session mint stubs
- Papering over sync cloud-header mint gaps — use async ownerFetch; see `syncHeaderGap.gate.test.ts`

## Messaging product E2E

Package unit tests cover crypto. Full dual-origin browse/messaging Playwright remains a **manual/local checklist** until a dedicated CI job exists. Do not claim messaging GA from unit tests alone.
